       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.     TCDLYAB2.
       AUTHOR.         C.I.HILLES.
      *INSTALLATION.   GOODYEAR TIRE & RUBBER COMPANY.
       DATE-WRITTEN.   OCTOBER 6,1980.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *SECURITY.       THIS PROGRAM IS UNDER NO SECURITY.
      *REMARKS.        THIS SORT PROGRAM GENERATES A LIST OF DAILY
      *                ACTIVITIES ON STORES DATABASE, GENERATED FROM
      *                FILE ABSTFIL2.
      *     DEC. 28, 1981
      *       1. MODIFIED LOGIC TO PRINT WITHDRAWALS AND RETURNS
      *          TOGETHER SORTED BY DEPT. CHARGED. RETURNS WILL SHOW
      *          A NEGATIVE AMT. CHARGED.
      *              KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *     ON FEBRUARY 23, 1982, DDAILY-TC-CODES 350 AND 351 WERE ADDED.
      *     TRANSACTION CODE 350 WILL REPLACE TRANSACTION CODE 326 WHICH
      *     IS THE ADDITION OF FREIGHT INFORMATION.  TRANSACTION CODE 351
      *     IF THE CORRECTION OF FREIGHT INFORMATION.  LMB.
      *
      *     APRIL 19, 1982
      *        1.  ADDED 2 NEW TC CODES (334 CODE TRANSFER) AND
      *            (331 RETURN WITH VALUE).
      *               KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *     ON JUNE 14, 1982, DDAILY-TC-CODES 327 AND 328 WERE ADDED.
      *     TRANSACTION CODE 327 IS FOR ANY C-ORDERS WHOSE PRICE UM IS DIF-
      *     FERENT THAN THE ORDERED UM.  TRANSACTION 328 IS THE CORRECTION
      *     OF THE 327 TRANSACTION.  LMB.
      *
      *     ON JULY 29, 1982, DDAILY-TC-CODES 352 AND 353 WERE ADDED.
      *     TRANS CODE 352 IS AN ADDITIONAL FREIGHT INFORMATION RECORD
      *     (350 IS THE FIRST FREIGHT RECORD).  TRANSACTION 353 IS THE COR-
      *     RECTION TO THE 352 TRANSACTION.  LMB.
      *
      *     MARCH, 1983, CHANGED THE PRINTOUT TO MATCH XCDLYABS.  THIS
      *     IS ADDING "NON-CODED PURCHASE ORDER ITEMS", "NON-CODED
      *     RECEIPTS AT DOCK", SEPERATING OUT "PURCHASE ORDER ITEM
      *     MODIFICATIONS" AND "RECEIPT AT DOCK CORRECTIONS" (AND ADDING
      *     THE NON-CODED COUNTERPART FOR THESE MODIFY TRANSACTIONS).
      *     CIH.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 25, 1983, ADDED THE HIGH USAGE TRANSACTION CODE
      *    NUMBER 399.  THE PROGRAM WILL PRINT IT'S DATA OUT.  LMB.
      *
      *    JULY 7, 1983.  CAK.
      *    MODIFIED TO BE A SUBPROGRAM ALONG WITH ALL ACTIVITY
      *    REPORT PROGRAMS.  A HEADER PAGE WAS ADDED. THIS NOW
      *    RUNS BY SELECTING OPTION #1 ON THE SCREEN BROUGHT UP
      *    BY R9 ON THE REPORT MENU.
      *
      *    ON NOVEMBER 14, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *       1.  MADE THIS SUBPROGRAM FLEXIBLE TO PRODUCE 3 KINDS
      *           OF REPORTS:
      *             -  REPRINT OF ALL TRANSACTIONS
      *             -  REPRINT OF ISSUES AND RETURNS SORTED AND CONTROL
      *                BREAK ON CHARGED DEPT
      *             -  REPRINT OF ISSUES AND RETURNS SORTED AND CONTROL
      *                BREAK ON REQUESTING DEPT
      *           THIS ELIMINATES THE TWO SUBPROGRAMS "TCDLYCHG"
      *           AND "TCDLYREQ", WHICH USED TO DO THE LATTER TWO
      *           REPORTS.
      *
      *      2. MADE THIS SUBPROGRAM FLEXIBLE TO REPORT FROM ANY
      *        GENERATION OF THE TRANSACTION FILE "ABSTFILE".  THIS
      *        IS SO THAT THE "REPRINT OF DAILY ACTIVITIES" CAN BE
      *        GENERATED FROM ABSTFIL2, THE CUTOFF CAN CALL THIS
      *        SUBPROGRAM AND GENERATE A REPORT FROM ABSTFILE, ETC.
      *        (ALL PRINT LOGIC WILL BE TAKEN OUT OF "XCDLYABS" -
      *        THE CUTTOFF PROGRAM - AND WILL BE REPLACED BY A
      *       CALL TO THIS SUBPROGRAM).
      *
      *     3.  ADDED THE ID NUMBER 6 TO THE 311 TRANSACTION (MODIFY
      *         HIGH USAGE AREAS), AND ADDED THE REQUISITION NUMBER
      *         TO THE PO ITEM TRANSACTION PRINTOUT.
      *         CIH.
      *
      *    ON MARCH 3, 1985, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO SKIP "999"
      *    TRANSACTIONS SO THEY WILL NOT SHOW UP UNDER "INVALID
      *    TRANSACTIONS".  THESE TRANSACTIONS CONTAIN THE FINAL ONHAND
      *    VALUE FOR ANY CODE THAT HAS HAD ACTIVITY.  A HEADER AND
      *    PRINT ROUTINE HAS BEEN INCLUDED IN CASE WE WISH TO PRINT
      *    THESE TRANSACTIONS AT SOME TIME IN THE FUTURE.  CIH.
      *
      *    ADDED INTERNATIONAL DATE ROUTINE "TDATECHK" ON
      *    MAY 16, 1985.    V.W.D.
      *
      *       DECEMBER 1985.  ADDED CODE TO PRODUCE A TOTAL PAGE FOR
      *        360 TRANSACTIONS.  SORTED BY BUDGET NO.  DALE H.
      *
      *    03/20/86.
      *       ADDED THE DEFAULT EXPENSE CLASS TO THE PRINTOUT OF
      *       ADJUSTMENTS (332).  CIH.
      *
      *    05/22/86.
      *       ADDED A DISPLAY OF THE FILE STATEMENT THAT DIRECTS
      *       THE PROGRAM TO THE CORRECT GENERATION OF "ABSTFILE".
      *       THIS HELP ME SOLVE A PROBLEM WITH THE PRINTOUT, AND
      *       MAY BE HELPFUL IN THE FUTURE.  CIH.
      *
      *    07/08/86                                     BARBARA WINTER.
      *       CHANGED PURCHASING TRANSACTIONS 320, 321, 360, AND 361 TO
      *       MATCH THE NEW PURCHASING PROGRAMS.  ALSO ADDED PO AND RLSE
      *       TO FREIGHT REPORT.
      *
      *    02/02/87
      *       CHANGED ALL MONEY FIELDS TO 9(11)V9(4) AS WELL AS ALL OF
      *       THE REPORT FORMATS TO COINCIDE WITH THESE CHANGES. THE
      *       PROGRAM NOW USES DATA SET BUFFER DESCRIPTIONS FROM
      *       COPYLIB.  BJP.
      *
      *C  09/21/1992    DAVE PLUM     REQUEST #6261
      *C  ADDED TC 326 AS A VALID TRANSACTION.  TC 326
      *C  IS DOCK RECEIPT ACCOUNTING DATA.
      *C
      *C  11/23/1993     BK DISMUKES    REQUEST #6444
      *C    ADDED LOGIC TO REMOVE ZERO STOREROOM ADJUSTMENTS FROM
      *C    THE DAILY ABS REPORT.  ALSO ADDED LOGIC TO PAGE BREAK
      *C    ON NEW PRODUCTION DATE.
      *C
      *C  11/30/1993     BK DISMUKES    REQUEST #6447
      *C    ADDED LOGIC TO FLAG STOREROOM CODES WITH ZERO ON HAND,
      *C    BELOW REORDER POINT, OR BELOW EXPEDITE POINT.
      *C
      *C  07JAN1994      DAVE PLUM      REQUEST #6461
      *C  MADE 2 REVISIONS TO THE FREIGHT RECORD PROCESSING, FOUND
      *C  IN THE 96XX PARAGRAPHS, TO STOP PARAGRAPH 9990-REFORMAT
      *C  FROM BEING EXECUTED WHEN EXACTLY ZERO RECORDS ARE SORTED.
      *C
      *C  07/26/94       CR KALMAN      REQUEST #94-014 & #6521
      *C  ADDED A COLUMN FOR UNIT PRICE AND A COLUMN FOR MATERIAL
      *C  EXTENSION TO THE REPORTS TITLED "DAILY NON-CODED RECEIPTS
      *C  AT DOCK" AND "DAILY CODED RECEIPTS AT DOCK".  ALSO ADDED
      *C  FIELDS FOR TOTAL NON-CODED RECEIPTS, TOTAL CODED RECEIPTS
      *C  AND TOTAL WITHDRAWALS AND RETURNS TO THE "DAILY TRANSACTION
      *C  COUNTS" REPORT.
      *C
      *C  09/19/94       JS BUNGO
      *C  ADDED NEW TRANSACTIONS 341 AND 342.  THESE TRANSACTIONS
      *C  CONTAIN CHAT NUMBER INFORMATION AND WILL PASSED ON TO
      *C  THE CHESS CORPORATE SYSTEM.
      *C
      *C  06/19/95       JS BUNGO
      *C  ADDED NEW TRANSACTION 923 AND 924.  THESE TRANSACTIONS
      *C  CONTAIN THE DECIMAL VALUE OF THE QTY DLVR IN A TRANSACTION
      *C  323 OR 324.
      *C
      *C  06/19/95       JS BUNGO
      *C  ADDED NEW TRANSACTIONS 523, 524, 623, AND 624.  THESE
      *C  TRANSACTIONS NEED TO BE CONVERTED TO A 323 FOR REPORTING.
      *C  THESE TRANSACTIONS ARE THE BATCH VERSION OF 323, 324,
      *C  423 AND 424 RESPECTIVELY.
      *C
      *C  13SEP1995      DAVE PLUM     REQUEST #6585
      *C  REVISED LOGIC TO INSURE THAT DATE-MODE = "4" FOR CALLS TO
      *C  TDATECHK WHEN CONVERTING A TRANSACTION DATE INTO A DATE
      *C  SUITABLE FOR PRINTING.  ALL TC 311 RECORDS WERE BEING
      *C  PRINTED WITH THE CURRENT DATE (DATE-MODE = "1"), AS WAS THE
      *C  FIRST RECORD FOR A TC GREATER THAN 311 (LIKE 32D), BEFORE
      *C  THE DATE-MODE VALUE WAS CHANGED.
      *C
      *C  14SEP1995      DAVE PLUM     REQUEST #6586
      *C  REVISED LOGIC TO INDICATE THAT "MULTIPLE CURRENCIES ARE
      *C  POSSIBLE" IN THE DAILY TRANSACTIONS COUNT SECTION OF THE
      *C  REPORT WHENEVER SAVE-CUR-CONV-SW = "N".  ALSO CORRECTED A
      *C  PROBLEM WITH THE MAIN REPORT HEADING WHICH WAS USING THE
      *C  FIELD MPLTINFO-PLT-NAME.  IN PRACTICE THIS FIELD MAY
      *C  CONTAIN EITHER THE PLANT NAME (VALLEYFIELD, TOPEKA) OR THE
      *C  FIRST LINE OF THE PLANT'S ADDRESS ('8 GOODYEAR A',
      *C  'R.R. #7, GOO'), SO IT DOESN'T REALLY MAKE A GOOD
      *C  HEADING.  THEREFORE, ONLY THE 3 DIGIT PLANT CODE WILL BE
      *C  USED IN THE MAIN HEADING.
      *C
      *C  16NOV1995       CATHY YODER
      *C  ADDED "937" TO THE LIST OF VALID TRANSACTIONS.  THESE
      *C  TRANSACTIONS CONTAIN REQUISITION INFORMATION TO BE
      *C  SENT TO CORPORATE PURCHASING.
      *C
      *C  09/12/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C  EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C  RECOMPILE TO PICK UP COPYLIB CHANGES.
      *C
      *C  10/28/96  CA YODER    REQ # 96-006
      *C  CHANGED REPORT TO SHOW CLOCK CARD NAME IN ADDITION TO CLOCK
      *C  CARD NUMBER.  THE NAME WILL APPEAR IF THE PLANT IS VALIDATING
      *C  THE CLOCK CARD NUMBER (INDICATED BY A SWITCH IN MPLTINFO).
      *C
      *C  09APR1997   DAVE PLUM
      *C  REVISED THE CLOCK CARD NAME LOGIC ADDED ON 10/28/96 TO NO
      *C  LONGER BE DEPENDENT ON THE MPLTINFO SWITCH.  IN OTHER WORDS,
      *C  WE WILL NOW ATTEMPT TO OBTAIN THE CLOCK CARD NAME FROM THE
      *C  PERSONNEL FILE FOR EVERY CLOCK CARD NUMBER.  IF THE CLOCK
      *C  CARD NUMBER IS NOT FOUND IN THIS FILE, SPACES WILL BE PRINTED
      *C  FOR THE CLOCK CARD NAME.
      *C
      *C  10APR1997   DAVE PLUM
      *C  CORRECTED THE PARAGRAPH 9995-NUMERIC-CHECK LOGIC FOR TC352
      *C  TO HANDLE THE CASE OF "MULTI" FREIGHT RECORDS WHICH DO NOT
      *C  INCLUDE A NUMERIC WEIGHT FIELD.
      *C
      *C 07NOV1997    DAVE PLUM
      *C ADDED TC 300 AND TC 301 TO THE LIST OF VALID TRANSACTIONS.
      *C
      *C 23DEC1997    DAVE PLUM
      *C ADDED TC 354 TO THE LIST OF VALID TRANSACTIONS.
      *C
      *C 14JAN1998    CA YODER    REQ #97-022
      *C FOR THE FULL REPORT & REPORT BY CHARGE DEPARTMENT, ADDED
      *C EXPENSE CLASS TO THE SORT.  THE "WITHDRAWALS & RETURNS"
      *C PORTION OF THE REPORT IS NOW SORTED BY DEPT, THEN EXPENSE
      *C CLASS.
      *C
      *C 25MAR1998    CA YODER
      *C FOUND THAT 430 AND 433 TRANSACTIONS WERE BEING EXCLUDED
      *C FROM THE ISSUES AND RETURNS REPORTS.  INCLUDED THE
      *C TRANSACTIONS IN THE LOGIC TO SELECT THE RECORDS.
      *C
      *C 11SEP1998    CA YODER
      *C CHANGED CHECK TO SEE IF THE *OVER* MESSAGE SHOULD PRINT FOR
      *C T333-QTY.  IT WAS CHECKING IF THE VALUE WAS > 999999 WHEN
      *C THE FIELD COULD ONLY HOLD UP TO 99999.  SO THE *OVER* MESSAGE
      *C NEVER APPEARED IN PRT-333-QTY-R.  ALSO CHANGED LOGIC FOR
      *C PRT-399-QTY-R.
      *C
      *C 27AUG2003   BRUCE GEISER      TCM REQUEST
      *C IF "MULTIPLE CURRENCIES ARE POSSIBLE", STILL SHOW THE TOTALS.
      *C

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.    HP-3000.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.    HP-3000.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.      C01 IS NEW-PAGE.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MPLTINFO-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DDESC-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1401
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT PERS-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM0301
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT PRINT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.
           SELECT ABST-FILE  ASSIGN TO DISK-ABSTFIL2
             FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.
           SELECT SORT-FILE  ASSIGN TO DISK-SORT.
      *    SELECT SORT-360-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-SRTFILE.
      *    SELECT WORK-360-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-DWRKFIL.
           SELECT SORT-FRT-FILE ASSIGN TO DISK-SRTFRTFL.
           SELECT FRT-FILE-IN  ASSIGN TO  DISK-FRTINFIL.
           SELECT FRT-FILE-OUT ASSIGN TO  DISK-FRTOUTFL.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  MPLTINFO-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       FD  MSTORERM-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  DDESC-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DDESC-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1400  OF MCFLCS1401.

       FD  PERS-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  PERS-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPMM0300  OF MCFLMM0301.

       FD  ABST-FILE   RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS
                       LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
                       DATA RECORD IS ABST-RCD.
       01  ABST-RCD                 PIC X(80).

       SD SORT-FILE   RECORD CONTAINS 95 CHARACTERS
                      DATA RECORD IS SRT-REC.
       01  SRT-REC.
           05  SRT-DATE                  PIC X(6).
           05  SRT-TIME                  PIC X(6).
           05  SRT-TC                    PIC X(3).
           05  FILLER                    PIC X(3).
           05  SRT-CODE                  PIC X(7).
           05  SRT-ID                    PIC XX.
           05  FILLER                    PIC X(45).
           05  SRT-ISS-REQ-DEPT          PIC X(4).
           05  SRT-ISS-EMP               PIC X(4).
           05  SRT-ISS-FIELD-ONLY        PIC X(6).
           05  SRT-ACTUAL-TC             PIC X(3).
           05  SRT-ISS-EXP-CLASS         PIC X(6).

      *SD  SORT-360-FILE
      *        RECORD CONTAINS 20 CHARACTERS
      *        DATA RECORD IS SORT-360-RECORD.
      *01  SORT-360-RECORD.
      *    05  S-BUDGET-NO               PIC X(12).
      *    05  S-BUDGET-AMT              PIC 9(8).
      *
      *FD  WORK-360-FILE
      *        RECORD CONTAINS 20 CHARACTERS
      *        DATA RECORD IS WORK-360-RECORD.
      *01  WORK-360-RECORD.
      *    05  W-BUDGET-NO               PIC X(12).
      *    05  W-BUDGET-AMT              PIC 9(8).
      *
       SD  SORT-FRT-FILE  RECORD CONTAINS 72 CHARACTERS
                          DATA RECORD IS SORT-FRT-REC.
       01  SORT-FRT-REC.
           05  S-F-TC                    PIC X(3).
           05  S-F-PO                    PIC X(13).
           05  S-F-CARRIER               PIC X(4).
           05  S-F-PRO-NO                PIC X(16).
           05  S-F-PRO-DATE              PIC X(6).
           05  S-F-CHARGES               PIC 9(11)V9(4).
           05  S-F-TYPE                  PIC X.
           05     FILLER                 PIC X(14).

       FD  FRT-FILE-IN     RECORD CONTAINS 72 CHARACTERS
                           DATA RECORD IS FRT-REC-IN.
       01  FRT-REC-IN.
           05  F-I-TC                    PIC X(3).
           05  F-I-PO                    PIC X(13).
           05  F-I-CARRIER               PIC X(4).
           05  F-I-PRO-NO                PIC X(16).
           05  F-I-PRO-DATE              PIC X(6).
           05  F-I-CHARGES               PIC 9(11)V9(4).
           05  F-I-TYPE                  PIC X.
           05  F-I-MULTI-ORIG-RS         PIC X(14).

       FD  FRT-FILE-OUT    RECORD CONTAINS 72 CHARACTERS
                           DATA RECORD IS FRT-REC-OUT.
       01  FRT-REC-OUT.
           05  F-O-TC                    PIC X(3).
           05  F-O-PO                    PIC X(13).
           05  F-O-CARRIER               PIC X(4).
           05  F-O-PRO-NO                PIC X(16).
           05  F-O-PRO-DATE              PIC X(6).
           05  F-O-CHARGES               PIC 9(11)V9(4).
           05  F-O-TYPE                  PIC X.
           05  F-O-MULTI-ORIG-RS         PIC X(14).

       FD  PRINT-FILE  RECORD CONTAINS 132 CHARACTERS
                       LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
                       DATA RECORD IS PRT-REC.
       01  PRT-REC.
           05  PRT-LINE                  PIC X(132).
      **************************************************************
      *    THE REDEFINES CLAUSE ENABLES US TO USE A SAME PORTION   *
      *    OF MEMORY SPACE ( PIC X(132)) IN MANY DIFFERENT WAYS.   *
      **************************************************************
           05  PRT-305 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-305-CODE     PIC X(7).
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-UM       PIC XX.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-ONHND    PIC X(9).
               10  PRT-305-ONHND-R REDEFINES PRT-305-ONHND
                                    PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-AVGCST   PIC X(16).
               10  PRT-305-AVGCST-R REDEFINES PRT-305-AVGCST
                                    PIC ZZZZZZZZZZ9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-REORD    PIC X(9).
               10  PRT-305-REORD-R REDEFINES PRT-305-REORD
                                    PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-MAX      PIC X(9).
               10  PRT-305-MAX-R REDEFINES PRT-305-MAX
                                    PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-305-EXPD     PIC X(9).
               10  PRT-305-EXPD-R REDEFINES PRT-305-EXPD
                                    PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(4).
               10  PRT-305-CLASS     PIC X(3).
               10  FILLER            PIC X(5).
               10  PRT-305-DEFAULT   PIC X(4).
               10  FILLER            PIC X(6).
               10  PRT-305-INVCYL    PIC X(5).
               10  PRT-305-INVCYL-R REDEFINES PRT-305-INVCYL
                                     PIC ----9.
               10  FILLER            PIC X(5).
               10  PRT-305-DATE      PIC X(8).
               10  FILLER            PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-305-TIME      PIC X(8).
               10  FILLER            PIC X(5).

           05  PRT-PLT-01 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  PRT-PLT-CODE     PIC X(9).
               10  PRT-PLT-ID       PIC X.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-PREV-CD  PIC X(12).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-AUTHOR   PIC X(10).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(2).
               10  PRT-PLT-CLASS    PIC X(3).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-TERR     PIC X(4).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-WD       PIC X(4).
               10  PRT-PLT-INS      PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-OE       PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-OR       PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-MR       PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-RLS      PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-SO       PIC X(3).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(29).
               10  PRT-PLT-DATE     PIC X(8).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-TIME     PIC X(8).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(9).

           05  PRT-PLT-02 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(13).
               10  PRT-PLT-DESC     PIC X(50).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(69).

           05  PRT-PLT-03 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(13).
               10  PRT-PLT-DISP     PIC X(30).
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-PLT-UM1      PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-UM1-CF   PIC ------9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-PLT-UM2      PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-UM2-CF   PIC ------9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(55).

           05  PRT-PLT-04 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(13).
               10  PRT-PLT-INVCYL   PIC ----9.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-PLT-E-LT     PIC ----9.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-PLT-FRCST    PIC --------9.
               10  PRT-PLT-REORD    PIC --------9.
               10  PRT-PLT-MAX      PIC --------9.
               10  PRT-PLT-EOQ      PIC --------9.
               10  PRT-PLT-EXPD     PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(59).

           05  PRT-PLT-05 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(11).
               10  PRT-PLT-AVGCST   PIC ZZZZZZZZZZ9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-PLT-STDCST   PIC ZZZZZZZZZZ9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC XX.
               10  PRT-PLT-MKTCST   PIC ZZZZZZZZZZ9.9999.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(69).

           05  PRT-PLT-06 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  FILLER                  PIC X(11).
               10  PRT-HIGH-USAGE-LINE OCCURS 6 TIMES.
                   15  PRT-HIGH-USAGE-LOC  PIC X(2).
                   15  FILLER              PIC X(2).
               10  FILLER                  PIC X(97).

           05  PRT-325 REDEFINES PRT-LINE.
               10  PRT-325-CODE     PIC X(8).
               10  FILLER           PIC X(4).
               10  PRT-325-QTY      PIC --------9.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(5).
               10  PRT-325-UM       PIC XX.
               10  FILLER           PIC X(5).
               10  PRT-325-PO       PIC X(7).
               10  PRT-325-DASH1    PIC X.
               10  PRT-325-RLSE     PIC X(3).
               10  PRT-325-DASH2    PIC X.
               10  PRT-325-RCVR     PIC X(3).
